            <p><strong>Why Arthavi?</strong> Unlike other platforms that push loans or require access to your personal
                email, Arthavi is built logic-first. It relies on secure, read-only CAS (Consolidated Account Statement)
                uploads for your <strong>mutual fund portfolio tracker</strong> needs and respects your privacy. It
                simply calculates your real XIRR without overhyping or selling your data.</p>
            <p>If you're still relying on spreadsheets like the <strong>google finance portfolio tracker</strong> or a
                <strong>portfolio tracker excel</strong> template, learn <a
                    href="/blog/excel-vs-portfolio-tracker/">7 reasons why Excel is bad for tracking stocks (and what
                    to use instead)</a>.</p>

            <h2>How to Track Your Investment Portfolio in India</h2>
            <p>Ready to get organized? Tracking your portfolio doesn't have to be a weekend chore. Here is the best way
                to consolidate your wealth.</p>

            <ol>
                <li><strong>Track all investments in one place:</strong> Bring your Zerodha, Angel One, Groww, and
                    Upstox investments into a single unified dashboard.</li>
                <li><strong>Use XIRR instead of absolute returns:</strong> If you are doing an SIP, absolute returns are
                    misleading. You must use XIRR to know the actual annualized profit of your cash flows. Learn <a
                        href="/xirr-calculator-mutual-funds/">what XIRR is here</a>.</li>
                <li><strong>Monitor asset allocation:</strong> Are you over-exposed to risky small-caps? Keep a tight
                    watch on your equity vs. debt split.</li>
                <li><strong>Rebalance regularly:</strong> Lock in profits and shift investments to maintain your target
                    risk profile.</li>
            </ol>
            <p>If you want to track investments for multiple people, check out our guide on <a
                    href="/blog/track-family-investment-portfolio/">how to track family investment portfolios in one
                    account</a>.</p>

            <h2>See the Difference: Real Portfolio Scenario</h2>
            <p>Imagine you invested ₹10,000 monthly in a mutual fund <a href="/sip-calculator/">SIP</a> for 3 years,
                and made a one-time ₹50,000 investment in a stock.</p>
            <div
                style="background: var(--card-bg); padding: 1.5rem; border-radius: 8px; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
                <p style="margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Expected Output:</strong></p>
                <ul style="margin-top: 0;">
                    <li>Total Invested: ₹4,10,000</li>
                    <li>Because of the staggered SIP investments, your <strong>Absolute Return</strong> might look like
                        a modest 15%.</li>
                    <li>But your <strong>XIRR (true annualized return)</strong> could actually be 24% because the latest
                        SIPs haven't been in the market long!</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <p>Without a tracker that understands dates and cashflows properly, you might make the wrong decision to
                sell a well-performing asset.</p>

